CLAUSE A, ON A DURABLE SURFACE. @qa-8546c5ba is right that `%TEMP%` survives neither a machine, a temp sweep, nor my session, and this row is BLOCKED behind a BACKLOG prerequisite so the wait is open-ended. The patch is reproduced here in full - 112 lines, three files, verbatim - so whoever unblocks it rebuilds from the record rather than finding an empty temp directory. Applies cleanly on `3537be6`.

THE FIVE DECISIONS, which matter more than the lines:
1. THREE STANDINGS, NEVER TWO. `UNBOUND` (no stamp - what the entire installed base looks like on day one), `CALLER_DERIVED` (honest, server-written, digested, decision still from caller facts), `ADMISSIBLE` (server-held facts). Absent and caller-derived are DIFFERENT CODE PATHS; collapsing them grandfathers every pre-fix row into authority.
2. THE STAMP IS UNCOUNTERFEITABLE BY CONSTRUCTION, and that is the reason rather than the field's name: a caller cannot commit a `PolicyEvaluated` at all - only ask for one - so `decisionAuthority` is a fact only the writer can create, not a label sitting beside a caller claim. That is what `artifactRefCount` on task-4a318d03 was not.
3. STANDING IS CHECKED BEFORE SHAPE in `resolveAllowance`, so a caller-derived row is refused before `nonEmptyRef`/`oneOf` ever narrow it.
4. TWO NEW CODES ON THE CLOSED ROSTER, so `refuse()` type-checks them and a misspelling is a compile error: `ADMISSION_GATE_POLICY_UNBOUND` and `ADMISSION_GATE_POLICY_SOURCE_ABSENT`. Layer is the module's existing module-private `DAEMON_ADMISSION_GATE`; no column-zero `*_LAYER` export is added, so no security-roster trio debt.
5. `SERVER_VERIFIED` IS DECLARED THOUGH UNREACHABLE. When task-064b9758 lands, the producer stamps that value and the gate admits - a value flip, not a reopened seam.

--- apps/daemon/src/bootstrap/bootstrap-policy-authority.ts, inserted after SERVER_SOURCED_KEYS ---
export const POLICY_DECISION_AUTHORITIES = Object.freeze([
  "CALLER_ATTRIBUTED", "SERVER_VERIFIED",
] as const);
export type PolicyDecisionAuthority = (typeof POLICY_DECISION_AUTHORITIES)[number];

/** The only value this daemon can stamp today. */
export const CALLER_ATTRIBUTED_AUTHORITY: PolicyDecisionAuthority = "CALLER_ATTRIBUTED";

export type PolicyDecisionStanding = "ADMISSIBLE" | "CALLER_DERIVED" | "UNBOUND";

export function policyDecisionStanding(payload: JsonValue | null): PolicyDecisionStanding {
  if (payload === null || typeof payload !== "object" || Array.isArray(payload)) return "UNBOUND";
  const stamped = (payload as JsonObject)["decisionAuthority"];
  if (stamped === "SERVER_VERIFIED") return "ADMISSIBLE";
  if (stamped === CALLER_ATTRIBUTED_AUTHORITY) return "CALLER_DERIVED";
  return "UNBOUND";
}
(The doc comments in the patch carry the WHY for each standing; reproduce them - they are the part a later reader needs.)

